# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts line endings on checkout by default, so every check
# printed a warning that a file would be rewritten with CRLF. Two of those files
# are shell scripts that run inside a Linux distribution, and a carriage return
# there breaks a comparison that looks correct on screen — it already did once, in
# a tarball listing.
#
# The repository stores LF, everywhere, for everyone.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose bytes must not be touched at all.
*.png binary
*.tgz binary
